All the bold, smoky flavors of cheesy chicken enchiladas simmered into an effortless slow-cooker soup. Fire-roasted tomatoes, red enchilada sauce, tender chicken, black beans, and sweet corn simmer hands-free before being finished with a splash of cream and sharp cheddar for a comforting restaurant-style bowl.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/recipes/a56797/crock-pot-chicken-enchilada-soup-recipe/).*

## Ingredients

### Soup Base
- ½ medium yellow onion, finely diced
- 1 teaspoon chili powder
- 1 teaspoon ground cumin
- 1 teaspoon garlic powder
- 1 can (19 oz) red enchilada sauce (mild or medium)
- 1 can (28 oz) fire-roasted diced tomatoes, with juices
- 1 can (15 oz) black beans, drained and rinsed
- 1 can (15 oz) sweet whole kernel corn, drained
- 2 lbs boneless, skinless chicken breasts, trimmed and cut into large chunks (thirds)
- 2 ½ cups low-sodium chicken broth

### Creamy Finish
- ⅓ cup shredded sharp cheddar cheese (or Monterey Jack)
- ¼ cup heavy whipping cream

### Optional Toppings
- Sour cream
- Fresh cilantro, finely chopped
- Fresh lime wedges
- Crushed tortilla chips or crispy tortilla strips
- Additional shredded cheddar or Cotija cheese
- Sliced jalapeños or diced avocado

## Instructions

1. **Assemble Ingredients in the Slow Cooker:** Place the diced onion into a 6-quart slow cooker. Add the chili powder, ground cumin, garlic powder, red enchilada sauce, canned fire-roasted diced tomatoes (with all their juices), rinsed black beans, drained sweet corn, and chicken broth. Stir everything together so the spices dissolve into the liquids.
2. **Submerge the Chicken:** Nest the trimmed chicken breast chunks into the liquid, ensuring they are mostly submerged in the seasoned broth.
3. **Slow Cook to Tender:** Secure the slow cooker lid. Cook on **HIGH for 3 to 3 ½ hours** (or on **LOW for 6 to 7 hours**). The soup is ready for shredding when the chicken is fully cooked (165°F / 74°C) and pulls apart effortlessly with a fork.
4. **Shred and Return Meat:** Use tongs to transfer the cooked chicken pieces onto a cutting board or shallow dish. Shred the meat into bite-sized shreds using two forks. Stir the shredded chicken back into the slow cooker.
5. **Melt in Cream and Cheese:** Pour in the heavy cream and sprinkle in the ⅓ cup of shredded cheddar cheese. Stir well to integrate the dairy into the warm broth. Keep the slow cooker covered on LOW or WARM for 10 to 15 minutes, stirring once, until the cheese has completely melted into a velvety, luscious broth.
6. **Ladle and Garnish:** Ladle hot soup into wide bowls. Let everyone customize their bowls with a dollop of cool sour cream, fresh cilantro, crushed crispy tortilla chips, extra shredded cheese, and a generous squeeze of fresh lime juice.

## Notes

- **Rotisserie Chicken Option:** You can substitute 3 to 4 cups of shredded rotisserie chicken. Add it during the last 30 minutes of cooking (on LOW) along with the cream and cheese to simply warm through.
- **Spice Level:** Adjust heat by choosing either mild, medium, or hot enchilada sauce, or stirring in a 4-oz can of diced green chiles or a dash of cayenne pepper.
- **Storage and Freezing:** Keeps refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 4 days. If freezing, freeze before adding the cream and cheese; thaw overnight, reheat, and stir in the cream and cheese right before serving.
